Message-ID: <52C16CAF.7080403@karssen.org>

Dear list,

I'm happy to inform you that ProbABEL v0.4.1 has been accepted in Debian
Unstable [1]. This means that ProbABEL will be available in the next
Debian release and also in upcoming releases of Ubuntu [2], Linux mint
and other Debian derivatives.
Note that the examples have been split of in a second package called
probabel-examples.

Many thanks to the people of the Debian Med team, especially Andreas
Tille, who mentored me through the packaging process.

To announce this to our wider community I'll draft a post for
www.genabel.org later today. In the mean time, I'll work on releasing
v0.4.2 (and package that for Debian as well).


Best regards,

Lennart.

[1] http://packages.qa.debian.org/p/probabel.html
[2] https://wiki.ubuntu.com/UbuntuDevelopment/NewPackages

